; xfail: error: unknown variant: Sqare
;
; args: -S --no-prelude
;
; Regression (2026-09-23): a `choose` whose `when` arms name the variants of a
; union the module cannot SEE (a record holding it was `use`d, the union was
; not). The union comes from the subject's TYPE, but both variant lookups went
; through the use-visibility gate: they answered nothing, the arm's tag stayed
; 0, and every arm tested variant 0 — the reader's switch carried `i8 0` for
; BOTH arms, and tscaly's printer answered null for every class at rc 0 until
; its module globbed the ast (lessons §3.5ji 2). The gate saw nothing either:
; "unknown variant" was reported only for a union it could resolve. The
; lookups ask again without the gate on a miss now, so the misspelt arm below
; is named — before, the compile passed in silence.
; A LIBRARY root on purpose: its modules' bodies are planned only when the
; library itself is compiled, and a module of a library is where the
; use-visibility gate bites (the same modules under a program root saw the
; union).
define xfail_when_hidden_union
{
    module shapes
    module reader
}
